    "description": "What: a Friend 'Squad' (Man Leader + Man 1-3) at (58-70, 80) marches east to (185, 80) with DangerAreas OFF (no halt drill). 'Field B', an own anti-personnel field Friend knows from the start (KnownAtStartSides), lies across the way at (130-150, 50-110); the route is priced known-mined x200, so the squad goes ROUND it - along its edge, the way a planner skirts any obstacle (CE-4655: the user saw a squad skirting a struck field blow up on mines laid right on the edge). Judge: (1) the squad marches; (2) the leader gets past the field (x >= 160); (3) no mine goes off; (4) nobody is hurt. Fail: a blast while skirting - the field's mines must keep off its edge (MinePattern.Laid, half a spacing, at least 1 m). Check: scripts/scenario-regression.sh mf-way-round"
  },
